The order's sparse line names lib/research, lib/, .tools/ and the CRO scan folder. My first canary dry run (18:46:40Z, cn3_canary_dry.out) read: REFRESH UNH_US_Equity status=SKIPPED_ALLOWED moved=model_rows,team_sheet ... reason=outside the allowed set: team_sheet. NOTHING was written (a dry run calls no write_one). Cause, read and proved: lib/research/corpus/team_sheet.py reads integrations/bloomberg/research/field_map.json (line 131) for the labels' descriptions, and that folder was not in my sparse set; I had also had to add org/standards (lib/opal_naming.py reads org/standards/NAMING_SCHEMA.json) a minute earlier. I added `git sparse-checkout add integrations/bloomberg/research` (git status 0 lines, `git diff 56bacbc853 HEAD -- lib/research` 0 bytes both before and after) and re-ran: WOULD_WRITE moved=model_rows guard=PASS (cn3_canary_dry2.out). The order's STOP clause names a dry run that is not WOULD_WRITE; I stopped at it, found the cause was my tree and not the world, fixed the tree and re-ran before any write. The order's sparse line should also name org/standards and integrations/bloomberg/research.
